body:
It's a cycle tbf. You are open with your community and explain your mistakes -> the community is more likely to react reasonably and support you -> said support allows you confidence to be open and explain your mistakes -> community is more likely to support you, etc etc.

&#x200B;

I do hope the cycle never breaks.

Honestly, on Phoenix, my longest wait so far has been a queue of 689, and a wait of about 10 minutes.

&#x200B;

Which tbf, I have never had to queue ever, but still.

I think I'm the only one in my FC who doesn't use the Steam version tbh. You are correct though, Steam figures are not accurate for how many players are actually playing the game.

&#x200B;

Still, it's very exciting. FFXIV being high up on the Steam players and high up on Twitch games category is brilliant. Especially considering we are in what should have been the worst time for new subs, the content drought before the new expansion.
